The marine and wind data come from Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com), used
under the Open-Meteo terms of use (free API for non-commercial use, fewer than
10,000 calls a day) and licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International (CC BY 4.0): "Weather data by Open-Meteo.com". Open-Meteo
builds them from the wave, ocean and weather models of national weather
services (Météo-France, ECMWF, DWD, NOAA and others). The widgets, the
configuration screen and the documentation credit the source, as the licence
asks.

The data are model forecasts, not observations: they are not fit for the
safety of navigation. Read the official marine forecasts of your national
weather service before going to sea.

